{
	title: 'Typed commands outrank passive completion; outside interaction dismisses',
	spec: 'Restore these invariants: passive autocomplete never substitutes a suggestion for a fully typed registered slash command, and a completion menu does not remain orphaned after focus leaves its interaction area. In the web command composer, plain Enter submits the original typed text when its command name exactly matches a registered command, regardless of arguments, passive highlighting, menu timing or candidate ordering. Thus /cd runs bare, /cd with an existing path submits that path, and /cd with a missing path reaches the command creation question. Do not normalize paths or validate arguments in the completion UI. For an incomplete command name, Enter accepts the highlighted completion without submitting. Explicit Up/Down menu navigation makes Enter accept that choice without submitting; editing the input resets that intent, and host replies cannot manufacture it. Tab and clicking a choice still accept without submitting; Shift/Alt Enter and touch keyboard behavior retain their existing contracts. The Enter hint reflects whether it sends or chooses. Terminal submission keeps its existing behavior. A pointer/touch interaction outside the message editor and completion popup dismisses the completion menu without changing typed text, selecting a suggestion, blocking the outside action or forcing focus back. Keyboard focus leaving this interaction area also dismisses it. Escape dismisses an open completion menu even when focus is outside the editor, without also pausing the session. Dismissal suppresses late replies for unchanged input; new editing can request fresh suggestions. Preserve keyboard access and popup choice clicks. Cover command Enter, explicit selection reset, stale replies, and outside/focus dismissal with focused behavioral regressions.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Completion receive deliberately reuses identical menus across inputs. Reset explicit arrow intent before prediction, not in host reply handling, so passive replies cannot create intent and edits cannot retain it. Keep intent only while the selected candidate survives. Use the registered command name only; send original arguments through the existing submit path without filesystem checks.',
		'Dismissal clears pending Tab intent as well as cached choices and suppresses unchanged-input replies even before a popup appears. Pointer and focus listeners scope the interaction to the textarea and popup (not Send/Attach); focus within the popup preserves native choice clicks. Touch Enter bypasses menu acceptance so the existing native newline contract holds.'
	],
	needs: ['1b']
}
